  "ledger_honesty_note": "REWRITTEN 2026-09-01 by seat claude-skipper-fix because the previous version was false and\na vault note had already repeated it to describe a client's page.\n\nWHAT THE OLD VERSION SAID:  stock_provenance_rows: 0, distinct 32, slots 32, every row\n\"harvest_or_prior\" - which a vault note turned into \"No stock photography at all. Every\nimage on our demo is his own work.\"\n\nWHAT WAS ACTUALLY TRUE, measured:\n  - 17 of the 32 rows named files DELETED by the 2026-08-14 unreferenced-image purge.\n  - 10 files on disk (the gallery set and the before/after pair) had no row at all.\n  - 11 of 12 rows that did name a live file recorded the WRONG SHA-256, because the\n    2026-08-25 smart-crop rewrote the bytes and nothing updated the ledger.\n  - The page was carrying a Dutch windmill at Keukenhof, an eastern-European lakeside\n    villa, a Pacific-Northwest culvert and a flat texture of grass.\n\nTHE LABEL WAS NOT EVEN WRONG ABOUT THE MECHANISM, WHICH IS THE POINT. Drainage1.jpg on\nthe owner's OWN published site is the same photograph as the old photo-service-3.jpg. It\ngenuinely was harvested. It is stock HE licensed. So:\n\n    HARVEST MEANS \"IT CAME OFF THEIR SITE\". IT DOES NOT MEAN \"THEY MADE IT\".\n\nThat is why this schema separates `source` (where the bytes came from) from `authorship`\n(who made the photograph). Only `authorship` may ever support a claim to a client or a\nprospect. `authorship: \"unverified\"` means NOBODY HAS CHECKED - it does not mean stock and\nit does not mean theirs, and it must never be reported as either.",
